# Third-party code in Dex

## OpenDia — `extension/`

Dex's browser extension is a fork of **OpenDia** by Aeon Inc.

    https://github.com/aeonfun/opendia
    Copyright (c) 2025 Aeon Inc
    MIT License — the full text is in extension/LICENSE.opendia

MIT permits the fork and requires the copyright notice and licence text to
travel with the code, which is what this file and `extension/LICENSE.opendia`
are for.

### What was taken, and what was not

Taken: `opendia-extension/` — the MV3 extension itself. Its background service
worker, its content script, and the page-understanding work inside them are the
part that is hard to write and easy to underestimate. Two thousand lines of
each, most of it about the ways real pages differ from the DOM you expect.

Dropped: `opendia-mcp/` — a Node server whose only job was to bridge that
extension to an MCP client over stdio. Dex's browser agent is already a server,
so it hosts the WebSocket itself.

That removes a process, a protocol and a port, but tidiness is not the reason.

**Tools arriving over MCP would bypass Dex's safety machinery.** An MCP tool is
opaque: it is called and it returns. Nothing classifies it, nothing assigns it
a confirmation tier, nothing verifies afterwards that it did what it said. On
that path, "post a tweet" would simply happen. Hosted natively, the same
capability goes through what every other action goes through — a confirmation
card before anything consequential, verification against the live page after,
and the rule that anything a page said is data rather than instruction.

### What this costs

Their anti-detection work for Twitter, LinkedIn and Facebook becomes ours to
maintain as those sites change; upstream fixes stop arriving for free. And this
is Dex driving the browser that holds the owner's bank and their email, rather
than a profile Dex signed into itself — so the blast radius of a page trying to
steer it is everything they are signed into. The untrusted-content rule covers
that and is restated in `extension/README.md`. Both were accepted deliberately
when this was chosen; they are written down so the choice stays visible.

### Changes made

Recorded in `extension/README.md` so the difference from upstream is one file
away rather than a diff away.
